modelica://Modelica.Math/conditionNumber:
Modelica.Math: conditionNumber (function)

Syntax    r = Matrices. conditionNumber (A);    Description  
 This function calculates the condition number (norm(A) * norm(inv(A))) of a general real matrix A , in either the 1-norm, 2-norm or the infinity-norm. In the case of 2-norm the result is the ratio of the largest to the smallest singular value of A . For more details, see http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Condition_number .    Example    A = [1, 2; 2, 1]; r = conditionNumber(A); results in: r = 3.0    See also  
  Matrices.rcond

Code:
function conditionNumber "Return the condition number norm(A)*norm(inv(A)) of a matrix A"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Function;
  input Real A[:, :] "Input matrix";
  input Real p(min = 1) = 2 "Type of p-norm (only allowed: 1, 2 or Modelica.Constants.inf)";
  output Real result = 0.0 "Condition number of matrix A";
protected
  Real eps = 1e-25;
  Real eps2 = 10 * Modelica.Constants.eps;
  Real s[size(A, 1)] "Singular values";
algorithm
  if min(size(A)) > 0 then
    if p >= 2 - eps2 and p <= 2 + eps2 then
      s := Modelica.Math.Matrices.singularValues(A);
      if min(s) < eps then
        result := Modelica.Constants.inf;
      else
        result := max(s) / min(s);
      end if;
    else
      result := Modelica.Math.Matrices.norm(A, p) * Modelica.Math.Matrices.norm(Modelica.Math.Matrices.inv(A), p);
    end if;
  end if;

</pre></blockquote>

