Syntax    r = Matrices. rcond (A);    Description  
 This function estimates the reciprocal of the condition number (norm(A) * norm(inv(A))) of a general real matrix A , in either the 1-norm or the infinity-norm, using the LAPACK function DGECON . If rcond(A) is near 1.0, A is well conditioned and A is ill conditioned if rcond(A) is near zero.    Example    A = [1, 2; 2, 1]; r = rcond(A); results in: r = 0.3333    See also  
