modelica://Modelica.Math/solveLinearEqua:
Modelica.Math: solveLinearEquations (function)

With simple examples this function demonstrates how to solve regular linear equation systems with Matrices.solve and Matrices.solve2, and how to solve singular linear equation systems with Matrices.leastSquares and Matrices.leastSquares2.

Code:
function solveLinearEquations "Demonstrate the solution of linear equation systems"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Function;
  import Modelica.Utilities.Streams.print;
  // solve and solve2
protected
  Real A0[0, 0];
  Real A1[2, 2] = [1, 2; 3, 4];
  Real x1_ref[2] = {-2, 3};
  Real b1[2] = A1 * x1_ref;
  Real x1[2];
  Real B2[2, 3] = [b1, 2 * b1, -3 * b1];
  Real X2[2, 3];
  // leastSquares and leastSquares2
  Integer rank;
  Real a[3] = {2, 3, -1};
  Real A3[3, 3] = transpose([{2, 3, -4}, a, 3 * a]);
  Real x3_ref[3] = {-2, 3, 5};
  Real b3[3] = A3 * x3_ref;
  Real x3[3];
  Real B3[3, 2] = [b3, -3 * b3];
  Real X3[3, 2];
algorithm
  print("\nDemonstrate how to solve linear equation systems:\n");
  // Solve regular linear equation with a right hand side vector
  x1 := Modelica.Math.Matrices.solve(A1, b1);
  print("diff1 = " + String(Modelica.Math.Vectors.norm(x1 - x1_ref)));
  // Solve regular linear equation with a right hand side matrix
  X2 := Modelica.Math.Matrices.solve2(A1, B2);
  print("diff2 = " + String(Modelica.Math.Matrices.norm(X2 - [x1_ref, 2 * x1_ref, -3 * x1_ref])));
  // Solve singular linear equation with a right hand side vector
  (x3, rank) := Modelica.Math.Matrices.leastSquares(A3, b3);
  print("diff3 = " + String(Modelica.Math.Vectors.norm(A3 * x3 - b3)) + ", n = " + String(size(A3, 1)) + ", rank = " + String(Modelica.Math.Matrices.rank));
  // Solve singular linear equation with a right hand side matrix
  (X3, rank) := Modelica.Math.Matrices.leastSquares2(A3, B3);
  print("diff4 = " + String(Modelica.Math.Matrices.norm(A3 * X3 - B3)) + ", n = " + String(size(A3, 1)) + ", rank = " + String(Modelica.Math.Matrices.rank));

end solveLinearEquations;

