Modelica.Mechanics: AbsoluteAngles (model)

This model determines the 3 angles to rotate the world frame into frame_a along the axes defined by parameter sequence . For example, if sequence = {3,1,2} then the world frame is rotated around angles[1] along the z-axis, afterwards it is rotated around angles[2] along the x-axis, and finally it is rotated around angles[3] along the y-axis and is then identical to frame_a. The 3 angles are returned in the range     -π <= angles[i] <= π   
