modelica://Modelica.Media/ShortPipe-2:
Modelica.Media: ShortPipe (model)

Model ShortPipe defines a simple pipe model with pressure loss due to friction. It is assumed that no mass or energy is stored in the pipe.

Code:
model ShortPipe "Simple pressure loss in pipe"
  replaceable package Medium = Modelica.Media.Interfaces.PartialMedium "Medium model" ;
  parameter Medium.AbsolutePressure dp_nominal(min = 1e-10) "Nominal pressure drop";
  parameter Medium.MassFlowRate m_flow_nominal(min = 1e-10) "Nominal mass flow rate at nominal pressure drop";
  Modelica.Media.Examples.Utilities.FluidPort_a port_a(redeclare package Medium = Medium) ;
  Modelica.Media.Examples.Utilities.FluidPort_b port_b(redeclare package Medium = Medium) ;
  // Medium.BaseProperties medium_a(p=port_a.p, h=port_a.h, Xi=port_a.Xi)
  //   "Medium properties in port_a";
  // Medium.BaseProperties medium_b(p=port_b.p, h=port_b.h, Xi=port_b.Xi)
  //   "Medium properties in port_b";
  Medium.MassFlowRate m_flow "Mass flow rate from port_a to port_b (m_flow > 0 is design flow direction)";
  Modelica.Units.SI.Pressure dp "Pressure drop from port_a to port_b";
equation
  /* Handle reverse and zero flow */
  port_a.H_flow = semiLinear(port_a.m_flow, port_a.h, port_b.h);
  port_a.mXi_flow = semiLinear(port_a.m_flow, port_a.Xi, port_b.Xi);
  /* Energy, mass and substance mass balance */
  port_a.H_flow + port_b.H_flow = 0;
  port_a.m_flow + port_b.m_flow = 0;
  port_a.mXi_flow + port_b.mXi_flow = zeros(Medium.nXi);
  // Design direction of mass flow rate
  m_flow = port_a.m_flow;
  // Pressure drop
  dp = port_a.p - port_b.p;
  m_flow = m_flow_nominal / dp_nominal * dp;

end ShortPipe;

