modelica://Modelica.Media/saturationTemp:
Modelica.Media: saturationTemperature (function)

Computes saturation temperature from (partial) pressure via numerical inversion of the function saturationPressure . Therefore additional inputs are required (or the defaults are used) for upper and lower temperature bounds.

Code:
function saturationTemperature "Return saturation temperature of water as a function of (partial) pressure p"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Function;
  input Modelica.Units.SI.Pressure p "Pressure";
  input Modelica.Units.SI.Temperature T_min = 190 "Lower boundary of solution";
  input Modelica.Units.SI.Temperature T_max = 647 "Upper boundary of solution";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Temperature T "Saturation temperature";
protected
  function f_nonlinear "Solve p(T) for T with given p"
  extends Modelica.Math.Nonlinear.Interfaces.partialScalarFunction;
  input Modelica.Units.SI.Pressure p "Pressure";
  algorithm
  y := Modelica.Media.Air.MoistAir.saturationPressure(Tsat = u) - p;
  end f_nonlinear;
algorithm
  T := Modelica.Math.Nonlinear.solveOneNonlinearEquation(function f_nonlinear(p = p), T_min, T_max);

end saturationTemperature;

modelica://Modelica.Media/enthalpyOfVapo:
Modelica.Media: enthalpyOfVaporization (function)

Enthalpy of vaporization of water is computed from temperature in the region of 273.16 to 647.096 K.  
Source: W Wagner, A Pruss: "International equations for the saturation properties of ordinary water substance. Revised according to the international temperature scale of 1990" (1993).

Code:
function extends enthalpyOfVaporization "Return enthalpy of vaporization of water as a function of temperature T, 273.16 to 647.096 K"
  protected
    Real Tcritical = 647.096 "Critical temperature";
    Real dcritical = 322 "Critical density";
    Real pcritical = 22.064e6 "Critical pressure";
    Real n[:] = {1, 1.5, 3, 3.5, 4, 7.5} "Powers in equation (1)";
    Real a[:] = {-7.85951783, 1.84408259, -11.7866497, 22.6807411, -15.9618719, 1.80122502} "Coefficients in equation (1) of [1]";
    Real m[:] = {1 / 3, 2 / 3, 5 / 3, 16 / 3, 43 / 3, 110 / 3} "Powers in equation (2)";
    Real b[:] = {1.99274064, 1.09965342, -0.510839303, -1.75493479, -45.5170352, -6.74694450e5} "Coefficients in equation (2) of [1]";
    Real o[:] = {2 / 6, 4 / 6, 8 / 6, 18 / 6, 37 / 6, 71 / 6} "Powers in equation (3)";
    Real c[:] = {-2.03150240, -2.68302940, -5.38626492, -17.2991605, -44.7586581, -63.9201063} "Coefficients in equation (3) of [1]";
    Real tau = 1 - T / Tcritical "Temperature expression";
    Real r1 = a[1] * Tcritical * tau ^ n[1] / T + a[2] * Tcritical * tau ^ n[2] / T + a[3] * Tcritical * tau ^ n[3] / T + a[4] * Tcritical * tau ^ n[4] / T + a[5] * Tcritical * tau ^ n[5] / T + a[6] * Tcritical * tau ^ n[6] / T "Expression 1";
    Real r2 = a[1] * n[1] * tau ^ n[1] + a[2] * n[2] * tau ^ n[2] + a[3] * n[3] * tau ^ n[3] + a[4] * n[4] * tau ^ n[4] + a[5] * n[5] * tau ^ n[5] + a[6] * n[6] * tau ^ n[6] "Expression 2";
    Real dp = dcritical * (1 + b[1] * tau ^ m[1] + b[2] * tau ^ m[2] + b[3] * tau ^ m[3] + b[4] * tau ^ m[4] + b[5] * tau ^ m[5] + b[6] * tau ^ m[6]) "Density of saturated liquid";
    Real dpp = dcritical * exp(c[1] * tau ^ o[1] + c[2] * tau ^ o[2] + c[3] * tau ^ o[3] + c[4] * tau ^ o[4] + c[5] * tau ^ o[5] + c[6] * tau ^ o[6]) "Density of saturated vapor";

  algorithm
    r0 := -(dp - dpp) * exp(r1) * pcritical * (r2 + r1 * tau) / (dp * dpp * tau) "Difference of equations (7) and (6)";

end enthalpyOfVaporization;

modelica://Modelica.Media/HeatCapacityOf:
Modelica.Media: HeatCapacityOfWater (function)

The specific heat capacity of water (liquid and solid) is calculated using a polynomial approach and data from VDI-Waermeatlas 8. Edition (Db1)

Code:
function HeatCapacityOfWater "Return specific heat capacity of water (liquid only) as a function of temperature T"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Function;
  input Modelica.Media.Air.MoistAir.Temperature T "Temperature";
  output Modelica.Media.Air.MoistAir.SpecificHeatCapacity cp_fl "Specific heat capacity of liquid";
algorithm
  cp_fl := 1e3 * (4.2166 - (T - 273.15) * (0.0033166 + (T - 273.15) * (0.00010295 - (T - 273.15) * (1.3819e-6 + (T - 273.15) * 7.3221e-9))));

end HeatCapacityOfWater;

modelica://Modelica.Media/enthalpyOfWate:
Modelica.Media: enthalpyOfWater (function)

Specific enthalpy of water (liquid and solid) is computed from temperature using constant properties as follows:

heat capacity of liquid water:4200 J/kg heat capacity of solid water: 2050 J/kg enthalpy of fusion (liquid=>solid): 333000 J/kg  Pressure is assumed to be around 1 bar. This function is usually used to determine the specific enthalpy of the liquid or solid fraction of moist air.

Code:
function enthalpyOfWater "Computes specific enthalpy of water (solid/liquid) near atmospheric pressure from temperature T"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Function;
  input Modelica.Units.SI.Temperature T "Temperature";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.SpecificEnthalpy h "Specific enthalpy of water";
algorithm
  /*simple model assuming constant properties:
  heat capacity of liquid water:4200 J/kg
  heat capacity of solid water: 2050 J/kg
  enthalpy of fusion (liquid=>solid): 333000 J/kg*/
  h := Modelica.Media.Air.MoistAir.Utilities.spliceFunction(4200 * (T - 273.15), 2050 * (T - 273.15) - 333000, T - 273.16, 0.1);

end enthalpyOfWater;

Modelica.Media: enthalpyOfWater_der (function)

Derivative function for enthalpyOfWater .

Code:
function enthalpyOfWater_der "Derivative function of enthalpyOfWater"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Function;
  input Modelica.Units.SI.Temperature T "Temperature";
  input Real dT(unit = "K/s") "Time derivative of temperature";
  output Real dh(unit = "J/(kg.s)") "Time derivative of specific enthalpy";
algorithm
  /*simple model assuming constant properties:
  heat capacity of liquid water:4200 J/kg
  heat capacity of solid water: 2050 J/kg
  enthalpy of fusion (liquid=>solid): 333000 J/kg*/
  //h:=Utilities.spliceFunction(4200*(T-273.15),2050*(T-273.15)-333000,T-273.16,0.1);
  dh := Modelica.Media.Air.MoistAir.Utilities.spliceFunction_der(4200 * (T - 273.15), 2050 * (T - 273.15) - 333000, T - 273.16, 0.1, 4200 * dT, 2050 * dT, dT, 0);

end enthalpyOfWater_der;

modelica://Modelica.Media/T_phX:
Modelica.Media: T_phX (function)

Temperature is computed from pressure, specific enthalpy and composition via numerical inversion of function h_pTX .

Code:
function T_phX "Return temperature as a function of pressure p, specific enthalpy h and composition X"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Function;
  input Modelica.Media.Air.MoistAir.AbsolutePressure p "Pressure";
  input Modelica.Media.Air.MoistAir.SpecificEnthalpy h "Specific enthalpy";
  input Modelica.Media.Air.MoistAir.MassFraction[:] X "Mass fractions of composition";
  output Modelica.Media.Air.MoistAir.Temperature T "Temperature";
protected
  function f_nonlinear "Solve h_pTX(p,T,X) for T with given h"
  extends Modelica.Math.Nonlinear.Interfaces.partialScalarFunction;
  input Modelica.Media.Air.MoistAir.AbsolutePressure p "Pressure";
  input Modelica.Media.Air.MoistAir.SpecificEnthalpy h "Specific enthalpy";
  input Modelica.Media.Air.MoistAir.MassFraction[:] X "Mass fractions of composition";
