Modelica.Media: specificEntropy (function)

This function calculates the specific entropy of R134a from the state record (e.g., use setState_phX function for input). The specific entropy is modelled by the fundamental equation of state of Tillner-Roth and Baehr (1994).

Code:
function extends specificEntropy "Specific entropy w.r.t. thermodynamic state | use setState_phX function for input if necessary"
  protected
    Modelica.Media.Common.HelmholtzDerivs f "Helmholtz derivatives";
  Modelica.Media.R134a.Common.PhaseBoundaryProperties liq "Properties on liquid phase boundary";
  Modelica.Media.R134a.R134a_ph.SaturationProperties sat "Saturation temperature and pressure";
  Modelica.Media.R134a.Common.PhaseBoundaryProperties vap "Properties on vapor phase boundary";
  Modelica.Units.SI.MassFraction x "Vapor quality";

  algorithm
    if Modelica.Media.R134a.R134a_ph.getPhase_ph(state.p, state.h) == 2 then
      sat.psat := state.p;
      sat.Tsat := Modelica.Media.R134a.R134a_ph.saturationTemperature(state.p);
      liq := Modelica.Media.R134a.R134a_ph.R134a_liqofdT(T = state.T);
      vap := Modelica.Media.R134a.R134a_ph.R134a_vapofdT(T = state.T);
      x := if liq.h <> vap.h then (state.h - liq.h) / (vap.h - liq.h) else if state.h >= vap.h then 1 else 0;
      s := liq.s + x * (vap.s - liq.s);
    else
      f := Modelica.Media.R134a.R134a_ph.f_R134a(state.d, state.T);
      s := R134aData.R_s * (f.tau * f.ftau - f.f);
    end if;

end specificEntropy;

