modelica://Modelica.Thermal/PressureIncr:
Modelica.Thermal: PressureIncrease (model)

Fan resp. pump with constant pressure increase. Mass resp. volume flow is the response of the whole system.  
Coolant's temperature and enthalpy flow are not affected.  
 Setting parameter m (mass of medium within fan/pump) to zero leads to neglect of temperature transient cv*m*der(T).   
Thermodynamic equations are defined by BaseClasses.TwoPort.

Code:
model PressureIncrease "Enforces constant pressure increase"
  extends Modelica.Thermal.FluidHeatFlow.BaseClasses.TwoPort(final tapT = 1);
  parameter Boolean usePressureIncreaseInput = false "Enable / disable pressure increase input" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Pressure constantPressureIncrease(start = 1) "Pressure increase" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealInput pressureIncrease(unit = "Pa") = internalPressureIncrease if usePressureIncreaseInput ;
protected
  Modelica.Units.SI.Pressure internalPressureIncrease;
equation
  if not usePressureIncreaseInput then
    internalPressureIncrease = constantPressureIncrease;
  end if;
  Q_flow = 0;
  dp = -internalPressureIncrease;

end PressureIncrease;

modelica://Modelica.Thermal/IdealPump:
Modelica.Thermal: IdealPump (model)

Simple fan resp. pump where characteristic is dependent on shaft's speed,
 torque * speed = pressure increase * volume flow (without losses)
 Pressure increase versus volume flow is defined by a linear function, from dp0(V_flow=0) to V_flow0(dp=0).
 The axis intersections vary with speed as follows:   
dp prop. speed^2 V_flow prop. speed  
 Coolant's temperature and enthalpy flow are not affected.
 Setting parameter m (mass of medium within fan/pump) to zero leads to negligence of temperature transient cv*m*der(T).
 Thermodynamic equations are defined by BaseClasses.TwoPort.

Code:
model IdealPump "Model of an ideal pump"
  extends Modelica.Thermal.FluidHeatFlow.BaseClasses.TwoPort(final tapT = 1);
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.AngularVelocity wNominal(start = 1, displayUnit = "rev/min") "Nominal speed" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Pressure dp0(start = 2) "Max. pressure increase @ V_flow=0" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.VolumeFlowRate V_flow0(start = 2) "Max. volume flow rate @ dp=0" ;
  Modelica.Units.SI.AngularVelocity w = der(flange_a.phi) "Speed";
protected
  Modelica.Units.SI.Pressure dp1;
  Modelica.Units.SI.VolumeFlowRate V_flow1;
public
  Modelica.Mechanics.Rotational.Interfaces.Flange_a flange_a ;
equation
  // pump characteristic
  dp1 = dp0 * sign(w / wNominal) * (w / wNominal) ^ 2;
  V_flow1 = V_flow0 * (w / wNominal);
  if noEvent(abs(w) < Modelica.Constants.small) then
    dp = 0;
    flange_a.tau = 0;
  else
    dp = -dp1 * (1 - V_flow / V_flow1);
    flange_a.tau * w = -dp * V_flow;
  end if;
  // no energy exchange with medium
  Q_flow = 0;

end IdealPump;

