ModelicaReference: 'partial' (class)

Prohibit instantiation of components of the class    Examples   partial block PartialBlock  input Real u;  output Real y;  protected  Real x;  equation  x = y;  end PartialBlock;  block Integrator  extends PartialBlock;  equation der (x) = u;  end Integrator;  block Gain  extends PartialBlock;  parameter k = 1;  equation  x = k*u;  end Gain;  model Composition PartialBlock block1; // Illegal Integrator block2; // Legal Gain block3; // Legal  end Composition;   Syntax  
See section on class_definition in the Modelica Grammar .   Description  
 The keyword partial defines that a class is incomplete and that it cannot be instantiated. For example, defining    PartialBlock block1;  
 is illegal. A partial class can only be used in an "extends" clause to inherit from it or in a "constrainedby" clause to define the constraints of a replaceable class.

